{{!-- The chrome every editable list on the Create-a-Site wizard wears: its heading, its optional
      suggestion chips and book prompts, its rows, and the button that adds one more.

      A BLOCK partial — the caller supplies only the rows, as `{{#> "stonetop.cs-list-frame" …}}
      …rows… {{/…}}`. cs-line-list.hbs and cs-pair-list.hbs are both this frame plus a row body:
      before it existed the wrapper, the label line, all five lines of the chips block and the add
      button were duplicated between them, so a change to the chip markup or to the add button's
      `data-list` contract was two edits and the one that got missed looked identical to the one
      that did not. That is the same trap cs-line-list.hbs was written to get the wizard out of,
      one level up.

      `label` is optional: the areas list is a column of titled cards and heads itself.

      Context: the caller's own, plus
        list        the `data-list` key the add button carries ("dangers")
        label       optional heading
        hint        optional parenthetical beside the heading, WITHOUT its brackets
        chips       optional click-to-fill suggestions ({list, text, used})
        kinds       optional book prompts, rendered as a static hint list
        addLabel    the add button's wording ("Add danger")
        frameClass  optional extra class on the wrapper (areas space their cards wider)

      Every one of those names is cleared off the dialog's own context before rendering (see
      _PARTIAL_PARAMS in create-site-dialog.js): Handlebars MERGES a partial's hash into the
      enclosing context, so a bare `chips` up there would be inherited by every list that was not
      passed one. --}}
<div class="stonetop-cf-gear {{frameClass}}">
  {{#if label}}
  <div class="stonetop-cf-pick-label">{{label}}{{#if hint}} <span class="stonetop-cf-pick-hint">({{hint}})</span>{{/if}}</div>
  {{/if}}
  {{#if chips}}
  <div class="stonetop-cf-chips">
    {{#each chips}}
    <button type="button" class="stonetop-cf-chip stonetop-cs-suggest{{#if used}} is-selected{{/if}}" data-list="{{list}}" data-text="{{text}}">{{text}}</button>
    {{/each}}
  </div>
  {{/if}}
  {{#if kinds}}
  <ul class="stonetop-cs-hint-list">{{#each kinds}}<li>{{this}}</li>{{/each}}</ul>
  {{/if}}
  {{> @partial-block}}
  <button type="button" class="stonetop-cs-add stonetop-cf-mini-btn stonetop-cf-mini-btn--add" data-list="{{list}}"><i class="fas fa-plus"></i> {{addLabel}}</button>
</div>
